{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "IR11682STRPBF",
 "kind": "switching_regulator",
 "manufacturer": "International Rectifier",
 "title": "IR11682S dual SmartRectifier driver IC for LLC half-bridge synchronous rectification",
 "source": {
  "document": "Datasheet No. 97476",
  "revision": "July 1, 2011",
  "pages": 22
 },
 "summary": "A secondary-side controller that runs two N-channel MOSFETs as synchronous rectifiers in a resonant (LLC) half-bridge, standing in for the two output diodes of a centre-tapped secondary. Each channel reads its MOSFET's drain-to-source voltage with a 200 V differential comparator, turns the gate on when body-diode conduction pulls VDS below about -140 mV and off as it rises through about -6 mV, near zero current. A fixed minimum on time, a blanking one-shot, cross-channel shoot-through lockout and a cycle-by-cycle MOT check that drops gate pulses at very light load make it robust. Gate drive is clamped near 10.7 V with +1 A / -4 A peak; switching up to 400 kHz; 8-lead SOIC.",
 "key_figures": [
