   "id": "llc-half-bridge",
   "title": "Typical connection diagram: LLC half-bridge with two synchronous rectifiers",
   "page": 1,
   "description": "The primary is a half-bridge, M1 over M2, across the input with a split capacitor pair C1 and C2 setting the other end of the primary at mid-supply; the switch node drives the transformer's primary through the resonant inductor Lr. The centre tap of the secondary is the output rail, filtered by Cout into the load. Each outer winding end returns to output ground through a rectifier MOSFET, SR1 or SR2, sitting in the low side. U1 reads each drain on VD1 and VD2 and each source on VS1 and VS2, and drives the gates through Rg1 and Rg2. VCC is powered straight from the output rail and decoupled to GND by Cdc.",
